      <link>https://om-intelligence.ch/projects/vocal-notation/vocal-notation.html</link>
      <description>📝 Re-attack sensitivity decides whether two same-pitch cells are one held note or two repeated notes. Sing repeated notes on separate syllables ("ta-ta") and it works; sing them legato on one vowel and nothing in the signal distinguishes them from a held note. The noise gate ignores anything quieter than the threshold; the tolerance rejects pitches further than that from a real semitone, which cuts slides and scoops.

